    "q-143288": {
      "dom_id": "step-q143288",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Given that ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{10}$ are I.I.D random variables, where\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}∼N(\\frac{5}{2},{1}^{2}),\\,1\\le i\\le 10,\n$$\n\nwhat is the distribution of $Y={X}_{1}+{X}_{2}+⋯+{X}_{10}?$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that if ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ are independent and identically distributed (I.I.D) normal random variables, where \n\n$$\n{X}_{i}∼N(\\mu ,{\\sigma }^{2}),\\,1\\le i\\le n,\n$$\n\nthen \n\n$$\nY={X}_{1}+{X}_{2}+⋯+{X}_{n}∼N(n\\mu ,\\,n{\\sigma }^{2}).\n$$\n\nTherefore, since ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{10}$ are mutually independent, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Y={X}_{1}+{X}_{2}+⋯+{X}_{10} & ∼N(10\\cdot \\frac{5}{2},\\,10\\cdot {1}^{2}) \\\\  & ∼N(10\\cdot \\frac{5}{2},\\,10\\cdot 1) \\\\  & =N(25,10).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-143288-a",
