    "q-143339": {
      "dom_id": "step-q143339",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Given that ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{15}$ are I.I.D random variables, where\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}∼N(0,{(\\frac{2}{5})}^{2}),\\,1\\le i\\le 15,\n$$\n\ncalculate $P(Y\\ge 1),$ where  $Y={X}_{1}+{X}_{2}+⋯+{X}_{15}.$\n\n*Hint: A table of values of $Φ(z)$ for different values of $z$ is given below, where $Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.5\\,$ | $\\,0.7054\\,$ | $\\,0.7088\\,$ | $\\,0.7123\\,$ | $\\,0.7157\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.6\\,$ | $\\,0.7389\\,$ | $\\,0.7422\\,$ | $\\,0.7454\\,$ | $\\,0.7486\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.7\\,$ | $\\,0.7704\\,$ | $\\,0.7734\\,$ | $\\,0.7764\\,$ | $\\,0.7794\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that if ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ are independent and identically distributed (I.I.D) normal random variables, where \n\n$$\n{X}_{i}∼N(\\mu ,{\\sigma }^{2}),\\,1\\le i\\le n,\n$$\n\nthen \n\n$$\nY={X}_{1}+{X}_{2}+⋯+{X}_{n}∼N(n\\mu ,\\,n{\\sigma }^{2}).\n$$\n\nTherefore, since ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{15}$ are independent and identically distributed, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Y={X}_{1}+{X}_{2}+⋯+{X}_{15} & ∼N(15\\cdot 0,\\,15\\cdot {(\\frac{2}{5})}^{2}) \\\\  & ∼N(15\\cdot 0,\\,15\\cdot \\frac{4}{25}) \\\\  & =N(0,\\frac{12}{5}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe wish to compute the probability $P(Y\\ge 1).$ We first convert $Y$ into a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y\\ge 1) & =P(Z\\ge \\frac{1-0}{\\sqrt{\\frac{12}{5}}}) \\\\  & =P(Z\\ge \\sqrt{\\frac{5}{12}}) \\\\  & =P(Z\\ge 0.65) \\\\  & =1-P(Z\\le 0.65) \\\\  & =1-Φ(0.65)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the $z$-table, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(0.65)=0.7422.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP(Y\\ge 1)=1-Φ(0.65)=0.2578.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
