    "q-152018": {
      "dom_id": "step-q152018",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "A sports shop sells table tennis balls in boxes of $6.$ The weight of a table tennis ball, in grams, is normally distributed with a mean of $2.72\\,\\text{g}$ and a standard deviation of $0.05\\,\\text{g},$ while the weight of a box, in grams, is normally distributed with a mean of $12\\,\\text{g}$ and a standard deviation of $2\\,\\text{g}.$ If one box full of balls is randomly selected, what is the probability that it weighs less than $30\\,\\text{g}?$\nYou may assume that the weights are mutually independent.\n\n*Hint: A table of values of $Φ(z)$ for different values of $z$ is given below, where $Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution.*\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.7\\,$ | $\\,0.7611\\,$ | $\\,0.7642\\,$ | $\\,0.7673\\,$ | $\\,0.7704\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.8\\,$ | $\\,0.7910\\,$ | $\\,0.7939\\,$ | $\\,0.7967\\,$ | $\\,0.7995\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.9\\,$ | $\\,0.8186\\,$ | $\\,0.8212\\,$ | $\\,0.8238\\,$ | $\\,0.8264\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "Let ${X}_{i}$ denote the weight of the $i$th ball, and let $Y$ denote the weight of a box. Then, we have\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}∼N(2.72,{0.05}^{2}),\\,1\\le i\\le 6,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\nY∼N(12,{2}^{2}).\n$$\n\nLet the random variable $W$ denote the weight of a randomly selected box of balls. Then, since\n\n$$\nW={X}_{1}+{X}_{2}+⋯+{X}_{6}+Y,\n$$\n\nwe have that $W$ is normally distributed, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[W] & =6\\cdot 2.72+12 \\\\  & =28.32 \\\\ \\text{Var}[W] & =6\\cdot {0.05}^{2}+{2}^{2} \\\\  & =4.015.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nW∼N(28.32,4.015).\n$$\n\nIn order to find $P(W<30),$ we convert $W$ to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(W<30) & =P(Z<\\frac{30-28.32}{\\sqrt{4.015}}) \\\\  & ≈P(Z<0.84) \\\\  & =Φ(0.84)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the $z$-table, we see that\n\n$$\nΦ(0.84)≈0.7995.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(W<30) & ≈Φ(0.84) \\\\  & ≈0.7995.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
