    "q-143362": {
      "dom_id": "step-q143362",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "A math test is composed of $15$ exercises. The time that a student takes to solve an exercise, in minutes, is normally distributed with a mean of $6\\,\\text{min}$ and a standard deviation of $2\\,\\text{min}.$ If one student is randomly selected, what is the probability that they will take between $80\\,\\text{min}$ and $100\\,\\text{min}$ to complete all exercises? You may assume that the times spent solving each exercise are mutually independent.\n\n*Hint: A table of values of $Φ(z)$ for different values of $z$ is given below, where $Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ | $\\,0.08\\,$ | $\\,0.09\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,1.0\\,$ | $\\,0.8554\\,$ | $\\,0.8577\\,$ | $\\,0.8599\\,$ | $\\,0.8621\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.1\\,$ | $\\,0.8770\\,$ | $\\,0.8790\\,$ | $\\,0.8810\\,$ | $\\,0.8830\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.2\\,$ | $\\,0.8962\\,$ | $\\,0.8980\\,$ | $\\,0.8997\\,$ | $\\,0.9015\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "Let ${X}_{i}$ denote the time spent solving the $i$th exercise. Then, we have\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}∼N(60,{2}^{2}),\\,1\\le i\\le 15.\n$$\n\nLet the random variable $W$ denote the time it takes a randomly selected student to complete the test. Then, since\n\n$$\nW={X}_{1}+{X}_{2}+⋯+{X}_{15},\n$$\n\nwe have that $W$ is normally distributed, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[W] & =15\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =90, \\\\ \\text{Var}[W] & =15\\cdot {2}^{2} \\\\  & =60.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nW∼N(90,60).\n$$\n\nIn order to find $P(80<W<100),$ we convert $W$ to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(80<W<100) & =P(\\frac{80-90}{\\sqrt{60}}<Z<\\frac{100-90}{\\sqrt{60}}) \\\\  & ≈P(-1.29<Z<1.29) \\\\  & =Φ(1.29)-Φ(-1.29) \\\\  & =Φ(1.29)-(1-Φ(1.29)) \\\\  & =2Φ(1.29)-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the $z$-table, we see that\n\n$$\nΦ(1.29)≈0.9015.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(80<W<100) & ≈2Φ(1.29)-1 \\\\  & ≈0.8030.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
