    "q-110258": {
      "dom_id": "step-q110258",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "In a certain shop, eggs are sold in cartons by the dozen.\nThe weight of an egg, in grams, is normally distributed with a mean of $65\\,\\text{g}$ and a standard deviation of $5\\,\\text{g},$ while the weight of an egg carton, in grams, is normally distributed with a mean of $50\\,\\text{g}$ and a standard deviation of $2\\,\\text{g}.$\nIf one carton filled with eggs is randomly selected, what is the probability that it weighs more than $850\\,\\text{g}?$ You may assume that the weights are independent.\n\n*Hint: A table of values of $Φ(z)$ for different values of $z$ is given below, where $Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,1.0\\,$ | $\\,0.8461\\,$ | $\\,0.8485\\,$ | $\\,0.8508\\,$ | $\\,0.8531\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.1\\,$ | $\\,0.8686\\,$ | $\\,0.8708\\,$ | $\\,0.8729\\,$ | $\\,0.8749\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.2\\,$ | $\\,0.8888\\,$ | $\\,0.8907\\,$ | $\\,0.8925\\,$ | $\\,0.8944\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "Let ${X}_{i}$ denote the weight of the $i$th egg, and let $Y$ denote the weight of a carton. Then, we have\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}∼N(65,{5}^{2}),\\,1\\le i\\le 12,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\nY∼N(50,{2}^{2}).\n$$\n\nLet the random variable $W$ denote the weight of a randomly selected carton filled with eggs. Then, since\n\n$$\nW={X}_{1}+{X}_{2}+⋯+{X}_{12}+Y,\n$$\n\nwe have that $W$ is normally distributed, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[W] & =12\\cdot 65+50 \\\\  & =830, \\\\ \\text{Var}[W] & =12\\cdot {5}^{2}+{2}^{2} \\\\  & =304.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nW∼N(830,304).\n$$\n\nIn order to find $P(W>850),$ we convert $W$ to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(W>850) & =P(Z>\\frac{850-830}{\\sqrt{304}}) \\\\  & ≈P(Z>1.15) \\\\  & =1-P(Z<1.15) \\\\  & =1-Φ(1.15)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the $z$-table, we see that\n\n$$\nΦ(1.15)≈0.8749.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(W>850) & ≈1-Φ(1.15) \\\\  & ≈1-0.8749 \\\\  & =0.1251.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
