    "q-114465": {
      "dom_id": "step-q114465",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "In a particular shop, eggs are sold in cartons. There are $10$ eggs in each carton. The weight of an egg, in grams, is normally distributed with a mean of $60\\,\\text{g}$ and a standard deviation of $5\\,\\text{g},$ while the weight of a carton, in grams, is normally distributed with a mean of $30\\,\\text{g}$ and a standard deviation of $2\\,\\text{g}.$ If one carton containing eggs is randomly selected, what is the probability that it weighs less than $653\\,\\text{g}?$ You may assume that the weights are mutually independent.\n\n*Hint: A table of values of $Φ(z)$ for different values of $z$ is given below, where $Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,1.2\\,$ | $\\,0.8849\\,$ | $\\,0.8869\\,$ | $\\,0.8888\\,$ | $\\,0.8907\\,$ | $\\,0.8925\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.3\\,$ | $\\,0.9032\\,$ | $\\,0.9049\\,$ | $\\,0.9066\\,$ | $\\,0.9082\\,$ | $\\,0.9099\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.4\\,$ | $\\,0.9192\\,$ | $\\,0.9207\\,$ | $\\,0.9222\\,$ | $\\,0.9236\\,$ | $\\,0.9251\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "Let ${X}_{i}$ denote the weight of an $i$th egg, and let $Y$ denote the weight of a carton. Then, we have\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}∼N(60,{5}^{2}),\\,1\\le i\\le 10,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\nY∼N(30,{2}^{2}).\n$$\n\nLet the random variable $W$ denote the weight of a randomly selected carton with eggs. Then, since\n\n$$\nW={X}_{1}+{X}_{2}+⋯+{X}_{10}+Y,\n$$\n\nwe have that $W$ is normally distributed, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[W] & =10\\cdot 60+30 \\\\  & =630, \\\\ \\text{Var}[W] & =10\\cdot {5}^{2}+{2}^{2} \\\\  & =254.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nW∼N(630,254).\n$$\n\nIn order to find $P(W<653),$ we convert $W$ to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(W<653) & =P(Z<\\frac{653-630}{\\sqrt{254}}) \\\\  & ≈P(Z<1.44) \\\\  & =Φ(1.44)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the $z$-table, we see that\n\n$$\nΦ(1.44)≈0.9251.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(W<653) & ≈Φ(1.44) \\\\  & ≈0.9251.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-114465-a",
